# Test: control-plane-protection (copp) under firewall backend vpp is refused at validate/commit.
# Question: does `ze config validate` refuse a `control-plane-protection` block
#           under `interface backend vpp` and `firewall backend vpp` with the
#           VPP firewall verifier's message through `firewall-producer-tables`?
#           A unit test cannot prove `copp`'s registered table builder is
#           invoked by `ValidateCustomSections` inside `ze config validate`.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-8 (copp) -- the
#            `firewall-producer-tables` original-tree validator translates the
#            `ze_copp` table and rejects its VPP-unsupported primitives at
#            validate and commit time.
# PREVENTS: a CoPP config passing commit under VPP and failing only during
#           daemon startup when `ApplyAll` rejects `ze_copp`.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
firewall {
	backend vpp;
}
control-plane-protection {
	bgp {
		rate 100/second;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=ze_copp
expect=stdout:contains=not supported by backend vpp
